delta-change "statements-suites"
message "StatementSuites: recursive statement and suite semantics"
author "ai"
doc "guide" """
  |# StatementSuites: recursive statement and suite semantics
  |
  |StatementSuites is a post-constitution Trellis product layered over VirtualLayout. It does **not** extend or mutate the frozen F0–F11 bootstrap constitution.
  |
  |VirtualLayout made virtual `NEWLINE`, `INDENT`, and `DEDENT` events consumable by ordinary graph grammar expressions. Its flat block example deliberately left one boundary open: a parent suite encoded every item as `Expr NEWLINE`, but a nested block already consumes the newline before its closing `DEDENT`. StatementSuites makes that ownership explicit rather than adding a parser preference.
  |

  |## Statement form is graph data
  |
  |Each production now has a typed `grammar.statement-form` edge to one of two first-class entities:
  |
  |```text
  |grammar.statement-form.simple
  |  statement terminates by consuming NEWLINE in its containing suite
  |
  |grammar.statement-form.compound
  |  statement terminates at its own closing DEDENT
  |```
  |
  |All pre-existing Bool0 productions are `simple`. `grammar.bool0.prod.block` is `compound`.
  |
  |This classification is syntactic metadata on productions, not a test on constructor names in Scala.
  |
  |## Suite is a first-class grammar expression
  |
  |StatementSuites adds `grammar.suite`. Bool0's block grammar becomes conceptually:
  |
  |```text
  |Block :=
  |  "block"
  |  NEWLINE
  |  Suite(field=items, sort=Expr, min=1, max=8)
  |```
  |
  |The suite expression points to:
  |
  |```text
  |sort        -> Expr
  |cardinality -> many
  |newline     -> layout.token.newline
  |indent      -> layout.token.indent
  |dedent      -> layout.token.dedent
  |```
  |
  |The suite interpreter owns `INDENT` and `DEDENT`. For each captured statement it consults the parsed production's graph-resident statement form:
  |
  |```text
  |simple   => parse Expr, then consume NEWLINE
  |compound => parse Expr, consume no parent NEWLINE
  |```
  |
  |No newline preference or constructor exception is built into the parser.
  |
  |## Nested blocks
  |
  |This source is now compositional:
  |
  |```text
  |block
  |  true
  |  block
  |    false
  |    block
  |      !true
  |  false
  |```
  |
  |The AST shape introduced by VirtualLayout is unchanged. `Block.items` remains `Many[Expr]`; nested blocks are simply nested `Block` trees.
  |
  |At a multi-level dedent the virtual stream can contain:
  |
  |```text
  |NEWLINE DEDENT DEDENT
  |```
  |
  |The innermost suite consumes its final simple statement's `NEWLINE` and its own `DEDENT`. The enclosing block is a compound statement, so its parent suite consumes no extra newline and can immediately observe the next `DEDENT` or statement.
  |
  |## Bidirectional printing
  |
  |Printing is the exact dual of parsing. A suite prints:
  |
  |1. `INDENT`
  |2. each item using its normal production
  |3. `NEWLINE` only for productions whose statement form is `simple`
  |4. `DEDENT`
  |
  |A compound nested block therefore leaves the printer at a line boundary without a fabricated separator.
  |
  |## Compatibility
  |
  |VirtualLayout remains independently materializable as `Language.virtual-layout`. Flat blocks are observationally equivalent between VirtualLayout and StatementSuites:
  |
  |```text
  |block
  |  true
  |  !false
  |```
  |
  |normalizes in both to:
  |
  |```text
  |block
  |  true
  |  ! false
  |```
  |
  |Lossless SourceProvenance source provenance and SourceMapLayout layout events are still preserved underneath the semantic suite stream.
  |
  |## Free changes
  |
  |`DeltaBool0` admits `grammar.suite` in its graph-defined replace/remove convenience operators. Suite bounds and structure can therefore evolve without changing host parser code. Statement-form classification itself can evolve with the already-free `connect`/`disconnect` generators by rewiring a production to a different first-class form entity.
  |
  |Invalid suite bounds, missing statement-form relationships, unsupported forms, and malformed indentation fail closed.
  |
  """
test "canonical delta contract"
  assert "canonical"
  assert "valid"
  assert "source-roundtrip"
  assert "dependency" "virtual-layout"
  assert "introduces" "grammar.component.statement-form" "grammar.component"
